 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Sat, 13 Jun 2026 16:31:21 +0000

grass-planetary-addons (1.0.0+20260613190000) unstable; urgency=low

  [ p.in.astropedia: OPUS / VIMS support ]
  * New opus= option: comma-separated OPUS API query params (e.g.
    instrument=Cassini VIMS,target=Saturn). Searches the PDS Ring-Moon
    Systems Node OPUS interface; -l lists matching observations.
  * New opus_id= option: download and import a specific OPUS observation
    directly (e.g. co-vims-v1590123456), bypassing the search step.
  * New vims_channel= option (vis|ir, default vis): selects which VIMS
    channel .qub cube to download and import. VIMS VIS = 96 bands
    (0.35–1.05 µm); VIMS IR = 256 bands (0.88–5.1 µm).
  * New helper functions: _parse_opus_query(), opus_search(), opus_files(),
    _pick_vims_qub(), _opus_id_from_row(), print_opus_results().
  * .qub added to IMPORT_BY_EXT (→ p.in.pds3) and PREFERRED_EXT.
  * _BODY_PATH_TOKENS: added saturn, jupiter, uranus, neptune (gas giants
    were missing; needed for URL body inference for ring-science products).
  * Companion .lbl label file is fetched alongside the .qub cube so that
    p.in.pds3 can locate the PVL header.
  * Downloads go to ~/RSDATA/<Body>/ (resumable via wget -c), consistent
    with the project download convention.
  * planetary.json written with sensor=CASSINI_VIMS, mission=CASSINI,
    body inferred from OPUS result target field.
  * Module description and keywords updated to mention OPUS/VIMS.

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Sat, 13 Jun 2026 19:00:00 +0000

grass-planetary-addons (1.0.0+20260613180000) unstable; urgency=low

  [ p.in.rings: FILTER_NAME support ]
  * New filter= option in p.in.rings: accepts the PDS3 FILTER_NAME string
    (e.g. CL1/CL2, RED/GRN, BLU/UV) from the image label; stored verbatim
    as filter_name under extended_metadata.planetary in planetary.json.
  * p_meta.py PlanetaryMetadata: new filter_name field; serialised in
    _build_planetary_block() and deserialised in _from_dict().
  * Testsuite: new test_filter_option_in_interface (interface test, always
    runs) and test_radlong_filter_name_recorded (SPICE-gated) in
    p.in.rings/testsuite/test_p_in_rings.py.
  * p.in.rings.md: updated USAGE synopsis and parameter table with filter=.

