grass-planetary-addons (0.8.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * p.in.astropedia: body inference for ~/RSDATA/<Body>/ now falls back
    to scanning the filename basename when the URL has no body path
    segment. Fixes USGS planetarymaps mosaics (Ceres_Dawn_FC_HAMO_*.tif,
    Lunar_LRO_LOLA_*.tif, Mars_MGS_MOLA_*.tif, …) which previously
    landed under ~/RSDATA/Misc/. The "Lunar" prefix is mapped to "Moon"
    to match the path-segment convention used elsewhere. Mission
    prefixes (LRO, MRO, Dawn, Cassini, …) are deliberately NOT mapped
    to bodies — those could be ambiguous (e.g. Cassini imaged many
    Saturnian moons).

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Thu, 04 Jun 2026 11:00:00 +0000

grass-planetary-addons (0.8.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * p.in.astropedia: after a successful import, the computational region
    is now aligned to the imported raster's extent and resolution via
    `g.region raster=<output>`. Without this fix, freshly-created
    projects (project= path) inherited a generic DEFAULT_WIND that did
    not cover the imported raster, so any subsequent `r.what` /
    `r.info` / `p.landing` call would silently operate on an empty
    window. On the auto-project branch the region is also persisted
    as DEFAULT_WIND (`g.region -s`), so the fix survives across GRASS
    sessions and the project is usable out of the box. On the DOI / LID
    / STAC branches the region is set for the current session only
    (DEFAULT_WIND of the pre-existing user project is left untouched).

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Thu, 04 Jun 2026 08:00:00 +0000

grass-planetary-addons (0.8.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * p.in.astropedia: remote COGs (http/https) are now pre-downloaded with
    `wget -c` (resumable, --tries=5) into a per-body local cache under
    ~/RSDATA/<Body>/<basename>, and r.import is invoked on the local
    copy. This eliminates the transient /vsicurl/ chunk-read failures
    that affected large HiRISE / PDS S3 tiles (e.g. TIFFReadEncodedTile
    failures at random row offsets). Body is taken from the catalog
    entry when cog=<key> is used, otherwise inferred from the URL path
    (.../mars/... -> Mars, .../moon/... -> Moon, etc.). Existing local
    files of the matching Content-Length are reused without redownload.
    For cog=<local-path>, behaviour is unchanged.

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Thu, 04 Jun 2026 07:00:00 +0000

grass-planetary-addons (0.8.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * p.in.astropedia: when project= is set and the project is built from
    the source's own WKT, force r.import to -o (override CRS check).
    The CRS match is guaranteed by construction but the WKT string can
    differ cosmetically (e.g. "Mars (2015) - Sphere / Ocentric /
    Equirectangular" vs "Equirectangular Mars"), which would otherwise
    trip r.import's strict WKT comparison and break the auto-project
    flow on real HiRISE / NAC stereo DTMs.

