grass-planetary-addons (0.8.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * p.in.astropedia: new project=<NAME> option. When set, the module
    probes the source dataset's CRS (via gdalsrsinfo for /vsicurl/ COGs
    or local PDS4 files), auto-creates a GRASS project at that CRS via
    g.proj -c wkt=..., switches the running session into it, performs
    the import, then restores the original project at exit. Removes the
    CRS-mismatch friction that previously bit users importing Mars MOLA
    (Equirectangular Mars) or other PDS-native products into non-
    matching working projects. The original /vsicurl/ + range-read
    behaviour is unchanged when project= is omitted.

