grass-planetary-addons (0.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New module p.in.astropedia (Python): fetch and import PDS4 planetary
    data products from USGS Astropedia STAC (stac.astrogeology.usgs.gov)
    or NASA PDS Federated Search API (pds.nasa.gov/api/search/1).
    - Accepts doi=, lid=, or search= as the discovery source.
    - Spatial pre-filter from active GRASS region (reads WIND via
      gs.region()); bbox forwarded to STAC and PDS API so only products
      intersecting the current map window are returned.
    - -r flag disables region filter for global searches.
    - -l flag lists results without downloading.
    - Import dispatched by file extension: .tif/.tiff/.fits -> r.in.gdal,
      .xml -> p.in.pds4, .img -> p.in.pds3.
    - -k keeps downloaded file; download_dir= sets cache location.
    - Testsuite: interface-description, arg-validation, and network-gated
      live STAC / PDS listing tests (skipped when offline).
  * debian/rules: SCRIPT_MODULES variable handles Python modules; they are
    installed directly from source (.py -> bin/<name> without extension).
  * Module count: 29 C modules + 1 Python module = 30 total.
  * README.md updated: v0.7.0, 30 modules, p.in.astropedia in table.

