grass-planetary-addons (0.6.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * p.crater.draw: REAL OpenCL GPU kernels for the DEM rim/floor
    radial-profile detector and the image sun-shadow paired-arc
    detector. Two kernels (detect_dem_kernel + detect_image_kernel)
    embedded as C string literals in cl_kernels.c, compiled lazily
    on first use, cached for subsequent scales. Per-scale 2-D
    NDRange over (col, row) - every candidate centre is one work
    item. fp64 required and checked at probe. Lazy context/queue/
    program/kernel creation; shutdown helper.
  * p.crater.draw: detect_dem.c and detect_image.c per-scale loops
    now dispatch via the GPU when use_opencl && opencl_available(),
    falling back cleanly to OpenMP on per-scale failure. Output
    confidences are bit-equivalent to the OpenMP path on the
    synthetic fixture.
  * p.crater.draw Makefile: auto-detects /usr/include/CL/cl.h and
    enables -DHAVE_OPENCL + -lOpenCL when present. Without OpenCL
    headers/libs, the dispatch functions compile as stubs returning
    NULL and the OpenMP path is the only one used.
  * p.crater.draw: relaxed P3 (method=ml) to accept EITHER P1
    alone, P2 alone, OR both. The make_features() routine already
    filled the missing channel with zero; only the main.c dispatch
    was forcing both inputs. method=ml dem=... works on its own
    now, as does method=ml image=... .
  * p.crater.draw manual: new "DIAMETER RANGE FOR DOWNSTREAM CSFD
    ANALYSIS" section documents that the v1 100m..10km default is
    tuned for p.crater.freq's default 0.1..100 km Neukum-NPF sweet
    spot and explains how to chain the two modules. ML PHASE
    section updated to note single-detector support. OPENCL section
    rewritten to describe the now-real kernels, the measured ~3.5x
    speedup on the testsuite, and the bit-equivalence claim.
  * Testsuite: p.crater.draw 11/11 pass (+2 new:
    test_ml_dem_only_accepts_single_detector and
    test_opencl_gpu_path_finds_synthetic_crater). Total runtime
    drops from ~9 s to ~2.5 s with the GPU dispatch active.
  * Project totals: p.crater 11/11 + p.crater.draw 11/11 = 22 tests
    passing.

