grass-planetary-addons (0.6.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Items 4 and 5 of the post-0.5.x roadmap landed.
  * Item 4 - P3 shallow ML detector in p.crater.draw:
      - New method=ml chains P1+P2 then rescores via a stacking
        meta-detector. 6 features per merged candidate (conf_P1,
        conf_P2, two squared-conf proxies, |diff|, mean).
      - Final score = sigma(linear combination), with weights/bias
        loaded from a .bin model file (magic "PCDM" + version + 6
        float32s + bias). When ml_model= is not given or the file
        cannot be parsed, the detector falls back to uniform 1/6
        weights - a documented baseline, NOT a learned model.
      - New ml_model= option.
      - Training pipeline (offline) documented in the manual:
        bootstrap positives from high-confidence merged P1+P2 outputs,
        random patches as negatives, fit logistic regression, export
        the 6 weights + bias to the .bin file. P3 learns from P1+P2.
  * Item 5 - OpenCL runtime probe in p.crater.draw:
      - New opencl_runtime.{c,h}. OpenCL device enumeration is real
        and prints platform / device name / version when built with
        -DHAVE_OPENCL -lOpenCL. Without HAVE_OPENCL (v1 default
        build), returns "no OpenCL support compiled in" diagnostic.
      - The detector inner-loop GPU kernels themselves are NOT yet
        wired; -c flag prints the probe and falls through to OpenMP.
  * Manuals: p.crater.draw.md gains ML PHASE (P3) and OPENCL sections.
  * Testsuite totals: p.crater 11/11, p.crater.draw 9/9 pass
    (+2: method=ml baseline runs, -c flag diagnostic runs).
    Project total: 20 tests passing.

