grass-planetary-addons (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Major: items 1-3 from the post-0.5.x development roadmap landed.
    Patch >= 10 triggered the minor bump (0.5.x -> 0.6.0).
  * Item 1 - Multi-ring basin aggregation in p.crater.draw:
      - New -m flag enables post-NMS grouping of candidates whose
        centres agree within basin_centre_tol (default 0.10 of the
        smaller radius) and whose radii differ by at least
        basin_ring_ratio (default 1.30). Survivors receive a positive
        basin_id and ring_index (1 = innermost) attribute.
      - New CLI options basin_centre_tol= and basin_ring_ratio=.
      - Output schema grows basin_id and ring_index columns (NULL
        when -m not set or when the candidate is standalone).
      - Manual MULTI-RING BASIN AGGREGATION section + FUTURE WORK
        sub-pixel centre-refinement note explaining the v1 caveat.
      - Two new tests: schema present + NULL when disabled, and
        smoke-test that -m completes without error.
  * Item 2 - Per-body simple-to-complex transition Dsc in p.crater:
      - PCraterBody struct grows dsc_km field; populated for Moon,
        Mars, Mercury, Venus, Earth, Vesta, Ceres, the Galilean
        moons (Io/Europa/Ganymede/Callisto), and Titan from Pike
        (1977/1980/1988), Schaber et al. (1992), Marchi et al. (2012),
        Hiesinger et al. (2016), Schenk (2002), Wood et al. (2010).
      - p_crater_simple_complex_D_body(g, dsc_km_measured) returns
        the measured value when >0, falls back to the 18 km * g_Moon/g
        analytic scaling otherwise. p_crater_final_diameter and
        p_crater_depth_ratio now thread dsc_km_measured through.
      - Manual gains a "Simple-to-complex transition diameter (Dsc)
        per body" subsection with the full table + sources.
      - New test test_per_body_measured_dsc verifies that a 6 km
        Mars crater stays in the simple regime (Dsc=7 km > Df=6 km)
        and reports dD_ratio = body simple value 0.150.
  * Item 3 - Hartmann (2005) isochron chronology in p.crater.freq:
      - 8 ages x 16 diameter cells of Hartmann's Martian production
        function tabulated as a (log-age, log-D) bilinear grid.
      - When -t flag is set, age is found by chi-square minimum of
        log10(N_obs) vs log10(N_Hartmann(D, age)) over 200 trial
        log-spaced ages from 0.001 to 4.0 Ga (Mars chronology range).
      - Hartmann mode falls back to Neukum NPF for Moon (no Hartmann
        calibration there).
  * Testsuite totals: p.crater 11/11 pass, p.crater.draw 7/7 pass.
    Total project test count: 18 (up from 15 in 0.5.9).

