grass-planetary-addons (0.5.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * p.crater.draw: new dd_simple= and dd_simple_map= options applied
    to detected polygons at write time. The per-polygon dD_simple
    value (sampled from the raster, falling back to the scalar, then
    to a per-body default lookup that mirrors p.crater's database) is
    baked into a new dD_simple attribute column on the output vector.
    NULL is written when the value is not set, so downstream tools
    can apply their own fallback. Output attribute schema grows the
    dD_simple column.
  * p.crater: when the input= vector carries a dD_simple column and
    the user has supplied neither dd_simple_map= nor dd_simple=,
    p.crater reads the column per-feature as the lowest-priority
    fallback. The four-tier override hierarchy becomes:
      1. dd_simple_map raster      (per-crater, highest)
      2. dd_simple scalar
      3. input vector dD_simple column (NEW)
      4. body database default     (lowest)
    This lets a p.crater.draw -> p.crater pipeline preserve terrain
    context across module boundaries without re-specifying the d/D
    inputs on each run.
  * p.crater.draw testsuite: two new tests
    (test_dd_simple_column_default_from_body, test_dd_simple_column
    _from_raster) verify both the body-default and raster-supplied
    paths. Test count is now 5 (was 3); all pass.
  * p.crater testsuite: test_dd_simple_map_raster added in 0.5.8
    continues to pass alongside the new behaviour. Test count: 10.

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Sun, 24 May 2026 22:00:00 +0000

grass-planetary-addons (0.5.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * p.crater: new dd_simple_map= option accepts a raster of per-pixel
    d/D values, sampled at each crater centroid (polygon mode) or
    impactor location (synthesis mode). Enables spatial variation of
    the simple-crater depth/diameter ratio across heterogeneous
    surfaces (e.g. Mars polar ice cap embedded in basaltic plains,
    Vesta HED boundary, mosaicked multi-terrain study areas). Sampled
    values are validated to lie in (0, 0.5]; out-of-range or NULL
    cells fall back to the dd_simple= scalar then the body default.
  * impactor_points.c: extended PCraterBodyCtx with fd_dd_map (open
    raster fd, or -1) so each synthesised ricochet/bounce uses the
    d/D appropriate to its landing site.
  * qtgrass 0.4.9: GrassCraterDialog "Geology && DEM" tab grows a new
    "d/D raster (spatial d/D variation)" combo populated from the
    current mapset's raster list. When non-empty, the dialog emits
    dd_simple_map= on the QProcess argv.
  * p.crater.md: new "Spatial d/D variation via a raster" subsection
    documenting the dd_simple_map= raster input and the three-tier
    override hierarchy (raster > scalar override > body database).

