grass-planetary-addons (0.5.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * p.crater: per-body depth/diameter ratio for SIMPLE craters added to
    the PCraterBody database. The 48 body entries now each carry a
    dD_simple field populated from peer-reviewed Pike measurements
    (Moon 0.196 / Mars 0.150 / Mercury 0.180 / Venus 0.140 / Earth 0.130
    / Vesta 0.180 / Ceres 0.170; icy moons 0.150; rubble-pile small
    bodies 0.200). p_crater_depth_ratio() and p_crater_depth() now
    take dD_simple as a parameter, smoothly transitioning from the
    body's simple value at D=Dsc to ~0.05 for very large craters
    in the complex regime. impactor_points.c receives the d/D through
    the new PCraterBodyCtx::dD_simple field. Resolves the audit
    finding that the lunar 0.196 was previously applied universally.
  * p.crater.draw: testsuite passes (3/3): --help check, binary-on-PATH
    check, and a synthetic-crater detection test that verifies the DEM
    detector finds the canonical 1300 m circular depression with
    centre within ~400 m of origin and D_eq within +/-50% (the coarse-
    stride scan inherently quantises to scale * stride/3). The earlier
    g.remove call cleaned up its outputs with a single multi-type
    pattern, which the GRASS option parser rejects; split into two
    calls.
  * qtgrass 0.4.9: new bespoke Qt6 dialog GrassCraterDrawDialog wraps
    p.crater.draw. Three tabs (Inputs / Detection / Run log) with all
    relevant CLI parameters, planetary-body picker, OpenCL flag, and
    QProcess-driven live output streaming. Wired into the Planetary ->
    Crater Analysis submenu as the first entry, above the existing
    Impact crater scaling and CSFD dating items.

