grass-planetary-addons (0.5.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New module p.crater.draw - automated crater-rim delineation from a
    DEM and/or a panchromatic image, producing a polygon vector ready
    for direct consumption by p.crater (input=) and p.crater.freq
    (vector= column=D_eq). Phase 1+2 of the design ships with:
      - DEM-based detector: multi-scale rim/floor radial-profile
        scoring (rim_mean - inner_mean)/(rim_std + 0.5), squashed by
        tanh into a 0..1 confidence
      - Image-based detector: sun-azimuth-dependent paired arc on the
        rim (bright vs shadow) plus rim-vs-interior contrast
      - Non-maximum suppression with disk-IoU, tagging method=merged
        when DEM and image agree on the same crater
      - OpenMP parallelism over candidate centres at each scale
      - OpenCL flag (-c) reserved; stubbed in v1 (OpenMP is used)
      - Diameter cap 100 m..10 km in v1; FUTURE WORK notes track the
        multi-ring basin aggregation (concentric circles sharing a
        centre point) and the >10 km basin-mode scaling roadmap
  * Project-wide license switch: all 29 modules and 7 libraries now
    carry the Unlicense (SPDX-License-Identifier: Unlicense) in their
    source headers, LICENSE files in every module/library directory,
    library README.md "License" sections updated, and debian/copyright
    now declares Unlicense for both source and debian/ files. Public-
    domain dedication makes the planetary tools maximally re-usable.

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Sun, 24 May 2026 17:00:00 +0000

grass-planetary-addons (0.5.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * p.crater: new impactor-points synthesis mode (forward only).
    A new impactors= option accepts a POINT vector with per-feature
    impactor attributes (velocity, impact_angle from local DEM surface,
    azimuth, density, diameter). Required companion: dem= raster, used
    to sample elevation and Horn (1981) 3x3 slope/aspect at each
    impact site. Five new col_* options let the user map their schema
    onto the expected fields; density_unit=kg_m3|g_cm3 toggles the
    impactor-density unit.
  * p.crater: oblique-impact crater morphology. For each input point,
    the module synthesises:
      - a circular polygon when theta >= 30 deg (near-normal impact),
      - an elliptical polygon (major axis along downrange azimuth,
        b/a = sin(theta)^(1/3) per Pierazzo & Melosh 2000) when
        5 deg <= theta < 30 deg,
      - a ricochet chain (primary ellipse + up to 4 bounces at
        4x the previous diameter downrange, with V *= 0.5 and
        L *= 0.6 per bounce, terminating when L < 1 m or
        V < 100 m/s) when theta < 5 deg (Schultz & Gault 1990).
  * p.crater: output vector grows new attribute columns: parent_id,
    bounce, kind, D_major, D_minor, azimuth_deg, theta_local_deg,
    elev_m, slope_deg, aspect_deg (in addition to the existing
    Df_pi, depth_pred, kinetic_J, tnt_kt).
  * p.crater: bit-exact ring closure for the synthesised polygons.
    The naive loop with i=0..N generated a closing vertex that
    differed from vertex 0 by ~3e-13 (due to sin(2pi) residual),
    which the GRASS topology builder rejected as an open ring. The
    last vertex is now copied bit-for-bit from the first.
  * qtgrass 0.4.9: GrassCraterDialog grows a 4th tab "Impactor Points"
    with the synthesis-mode toggle, point-vector picker, five column-
    name editable combos and a density-unit dropdown. The dialog
    validates that a DEM is set when synthesis is enabled and routes
    the right argv to the QProcess subprocess.

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Sun, 24 May 2026 16:00:00 +0000

grass-planetary-addons (0.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * p.crater.freq: enriched CSV output with per-bin histogram counts and
    power-law fit values. New output columns:
      - n_in_bin       raw crater count per log-spaced bin
      - N_cum_obs      cumulative observed density (unchanged)
      - N_npf_age      NPF curve evaluated at the estimated age
      - N_powerlaw_fit least-squares power-law fit value at the bin
    Header now records: body, area, N, estimated age (Ga), and the fit
    parameters log10(N) = intercept + slope * log10(D) with RMSE.
    The fit uses log-log least squares over populated bins; results are
    also surfaced in the run log via G_message().
  * qtgrass 0.4.9 grows a Chart tab in GrassCraterFreqDialog using
    Qt6::Charts (log-log axes via QLogValueAxis). Observed points,
    NPF curve and power-law fit are overlaid; title shows body name
    and age. The dialog stages a temporary CSV when none is given so
    the chart can always be rendered.
  * Optional PNG export: a new "Output PNG graph" field on the
    p.crater.freq dialog renders the chart at 4961 x 3496 pixels
    (A5 landscape, 600 dpi) via QChart::scene()->render() to a
    QImage backend, then saves PNG.
  * qtgrass build now requires qt6-charts-dev (added to debian/control).

