grass-planetary-addons (0.4.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * p.crater: fix inherited backward-scaling bugs from r.crater.
    The Pi-, Gault-, and Yield-backward formulas in r.crater used an
    incorrect substitution of W into the kinetic-energy expression
    (factor of 2 in (pi/12) vs (pi/24), and missing rho_p^0.22 in the
    Pi inverse), causing the projectile-diameter estimate to be off
    by ~11x for Pi-scaling at typical asteroid densities.
    p.crater 0.4.9+ uses cleanly-derived analytical inverses
    (substitution-based) for Pi and Gault scaling, and bisection root-
    finding for Yield scaling. Forward/backward roundtrip is now
    machine-precision exact.
  * p.crater: extended testsuite with Melosh 1989 reference values.
    9 tests cover module interface, body database validation,
    forward Pi/Gault/Yield against analytical Melosh eq. 7.8.4,
    forward/backward Pi roundtrip on Mars, Meteor Crater (Arizona)
    backward-mode reasonableness, two-layer depth-weighted effective
    density, and Pike (1980) simple-to-complex transition diameter.
    All 9 tests pass against the fixed module.

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Sun, 24 May 2026 10:30:00 +0000

grass-planetary-addons (0.4.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New module p.crater (Unlicense / public domain) merging and extending
    the r.crater grass-addon with:
    - Built-in planetary body database of 42 Solar System bodies:
      terrestrial planets (Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars), Moon,
      4 Galilean moons, 9 Saturnian moons (Titan, Mimas, Enceladus,
      Tethys, Dione, Rhea, Iapetus, Hyperion, Phoebe), 5 Uranian moons
      (Miranda, Ariel, Umbriel, Titania, Oberon), Triton, Phobos,
      Deimos, all 6 IAU dwarf planets (Pluto, Charon, Ceres, Eris,
      Haumea, Makemake), 5 candidate dwarf planets / large TNOs
      (Gonggong, Quaoar, Sedna, Orcus, Salacia), 10 visited asteroids
      (Vesta, Pallas, Hygiea, Psyche, Lutetia, Mathilde, Eros, Itokawa,
      Bennu, Ryugu) and comet 67P
    - body=custom slot for arbitrary user-defined bodies, requiring
      gravity, target_density, target_type overrides
    - Vector polygon input: per-feature equivalent-circle diameter
      D_eq = 2 sqrt(A/pi) from shoelace area
    - Optional surface + subsurface density rasters with per-layer
      thicknesses for depth-weighted effective density
      (excavation depth ~ Dat/3, Melosh 1989 §5.4)
    - Optional surface-type raster (1/2/3) sampled at centroid
    - Optional DEM for direct depth measurement (rim mean - centre)
    - Multi-method evaluation: Pi-, Gault- and Yield-scaling all
      computed and written as separate vector attribute columns
    - Simple-to-complex transition correction (Pike 1980) and
      depth/diameter prediction (Pike 1977)
    - Build-Depends adds pandoc for .md to .html stub generation
  * Module count is now 28 (was 27)

